{"event":"changes_requested","job_id":"docs-payment-methods-gift-cards-api-only","reason":"Full independent review of all 762 pinned raw lines with matching SHA-256. Candidate and suggestions match the accepted receipt; all five quotes are exact at their stated lines. The provider/onboarding boundary, balance brand-as-type versus payment giftcard-plus-brand, insufficient-balance /orders branch, asynchronous outcome, manual capture and simulator limitations are accurately retained. One narrow credential-identity error remains: the candidate and Q2 refer to sample PINs, but the captured form/request tables and samples specify card number plus CVC/security code (raw lines 72\u201374, 87\u201389, 351\u2013354, 369\u2013374). 'Invalid Pin' appears only as a simulated refusalReason for an amount ending (raw line 743); the page does not give a separate sample PIN field or PIN value. This matters for a reader selecting which credential to collect or send."}
{"event":"changes_requested","job_id":"docs-payment-methods-pix-recurring-payments","reason":"Full independent review of the 292-line pinned raw with matching SHA and five exact located quotes. The candidate correctly separates Journey 2/3, shopper-permission advice from required fields, token creation from immediate AUTHORISATION, scheduling AUTHORISATION from post-date CAPTURE/EXPIRE, retry timing, and the fixed-amount/example conflict. Two material plan-lifecycle qualifications remain: the summary says a minAmount plan can use a new amount without retaining the stated minimum and the shopper's ability to specify a maximum in their bank app (raw lines 93 and 167\u2013168); and it says to end a plan by deleting the token without saying the merchant must cancel its own billing plan, while tying recurring.token.disabled to bank-initiated deletion even though raw lines 269\u2013277 state that it follows token deletion generally. Q2 asks about charge and cancellation rules, so these summaries can mislead its answer despite the raw locator."}
